# __NAME__ plugin

Wraps __NAME__ as an MCP server for Claude Code and MyHub tenants.

## Configuration

| Variable | Required | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `__ENV_PREFIX___API_TOKEN` | yes | Bearer token for the __NAME__ API. Replace this with the real var name your upstream MCP server expects. |

## What's in the box

- `.mcp.json` — MCP server transport. The starter wires up the reference server `@modelcontextprotocol/server-everything` so the harness has tools to list right away. Replace it with your real upstream once you have it.
- `skills/` — slash-command instructions for narrow tasks.
- `agents/` — persona that owns this plugin's domain.
- `widgets/` — declarative dashboard tiles.
- `widget-elements/` — JS helpers (`$computed` functions, composite components, actions) referenced from widget specs.

## Local development

From the project root (one level up):

```
npm install
npm run dev        # widget harness on http://localhost:5173
```

The harness reads `plugin/.mcp.json` on start, spawns each server, and exposes its tools to the renderer.

## Publishing

When ready, copy this folder into the marketplace repo at `plugins/__SLUG__/` and add an entry to `.claude-plugin/marketplace.json`. Run `npx tsx scripts/validate.ts` from the marketplace root before opening a PR.
